From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:59:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] common, llama-bench: --oryon-profile runtime profiles

--oryon-profile balanced|throughput|low-power|auto|none (environment
BONSAI_ORYON_PROFILE) fills the generation / batch thread counts, the poll
level, an optional CPU mask and the barrier spin limit, but only for the
settings that were not given explicitly (-t, -tb, --poll, -C always win).

  balanced   generation and batch threads = all CPUs up to 4, else
             max(4, ncpu/2): on Snapdragon X (8 cores) 4 threads decoded
             2.8x faster than 8 in a desktop session
  throughput balanced generation, batch (prompt) processing on all CPUs
  low-power  half of balanced, no polling, yield immediately in barriers
  auto       the tuned profile written by bonsai-tune
             ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bonsai-oryon/profile, only if it was
             measured with the same number of CPUs), else balanced

auto is the default of llama-cli, llama-server and llama-completion; it
only reads a small file, there is no start-up measurement. llama-bench
applies a profile only when --oryon-profile is given. The chosen profile
is logged.

Part of Bonsai-Oryon (https://github.com/SatoruGoj0/Bonsai-Oryon).
---
